      "id": "emponb.1",
      "title": "Master Data Management",
      "parent_id": "",
      "icon_image": "storage",
      "description": "Reference masters driving selection lists, validations and cross-updates across onboarding.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_master_data_group",
      "obj_type": "-",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1",
      "functional_specs": "Group of reference master data transactions used throughout the onboarding process."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.1.2",
      "title": "Designation & Department Master",
      "parent_id": "emponb.1",
      "icon_image": "work",
      "description": "Maintain designations, departments, grades, cadres and design codes used by HR.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_designation_dept_master",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1.2",
      "functional_specs": "Header-only master with DESIGN_CODE, DESIGNATION_NAME, DEPT_CODE, DEPT_NAME, GRADE, GRADE_NAME, CADRE, CADRE_NAME, JOINED_AS, ACTIVE_FLAG. Codes unique within master; DESIGN_CODE mandatory and active to be selectable. Search, Add, Edit, Delete."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.1.3",
      "title": "Organisation Setup Master",
      "parent_id": "emponb.1",
      "icon_image": "apartment",
      "description": "Maintain employment site, payroll site, work shift and holiday table values used at confirmation.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_org_setup_master",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1.3",
      "functional_specs": "Header-only master with EMP_SITE, SITE_NAME, PAY_SITE, PAY_SITE_NAME, WORK_SHIFT, SHIFT_NAME, SHIFT_TIMINGS, HOL_TBLNO, HOL_TBL_NAME, ACTIVE_FLAG. Codes unique; only active rows selectable in finalization. Search, Add, Edit, Delete. Also captures PIN (site pincode) and STATE_CODE (validated against the State Master EMPONB_STATE_MASTER)."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.1.5",
      "title": "Qualification Master",
      "parent_id": "emponb.1",
      "icon_image": "school",
      "description": "Maintain qualification codes/types used in candidate education detail.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_qualification_master",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1.5",
      "functional_specs": "Header-only master with QLF_CODE, QLF_NAME, QLF_TYPE (Academic/Professional/Certification), COURSE_TYPE (Full-time/Part-time/Distance), ACTIVE_FLAG. QLF_CODE unique; QLF_TYPE mandatory. Search, Add, Edit, Delete."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.1.6",
      "title": "Demographic Reference Master",
      "parent_id": "emponb.1",
      "icon_image": "diversity_3",
      "description": "Maintain lookup values for Religion, Caste, Blood Group, Marital Status, Name Prefix, Mother Tongue, Nationality and Relation.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_demographic_master",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1.6",
      "functional_specs": "Header-only master with LOOKUP_TYPE, LOOKUP_CODE, LOOKUP_DESC, ACTIVE_FLAG. (LOOKUP_TYPE, LOOKUP_CODE) unique; only active values appear in candidate drop-downs. Search, Add, Edit, Delete."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.1.7",
      "title": "State Master",
      "parent_id": "emponb.1",
      "icon_image": "map",
      "description": "Maintain the list of Indian states/union territories used as a reference master.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_state_master",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.1.7",
      "functional_specs": "Header-only master on table EMPONB_STATE_MASTER with columns STATE_CODE (VARCHAR(10), primary/unique code), STATE_NAME (VARCHAR(100)), COUNTRY (VARCHAR(50), plain text, always IND — no Country Master/lookup per project rule), ACTIVE_FLAG (CHAR(1), Y/N, default Y). STATE_CODE must be unique. Business actions: Search, Add, Edit, Delete. Table is seeded with the standard list of Indian states/UTs and their codes."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.3",
      "title": "Candidate Onboarding Management",
      "parent_id": "",
      "icon_image": "how_to_reg",
      "description": "HR-facing master transaction covering the full candidate onboarding lifecycle.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_candidate_group",
      "obj_type": "-",
      "menu_path": "emponb.3",
      "functional_specs": "Group for the candidate onboarding record and its lifecycle actions."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.3.1",
      "title": "Candidate Onboarding Record",
      "parent_id": "emponb.3",
      "icon_image": "person_add",
      "description": "HR-facing candidate onboarding transaction: a header form on EMPONB_CANDIDATE_RECORD plus three detail forms - Past Experience (EMPONB_CAND_EXPERIENCE), Educational Qualification (EMPONB_CAND_EDUCATION) and Family (EMPONB_CAND_FAMILY), each linked to the header by CANDIDATE_ID and ordered by LINE_NO. HR initiates the candidate, generates an access key and sends the onboarding link, the candidate submits their details, and HR then marks the record for review and finally confirms the candidate as an employee, with STATUS moving Link Generated -> Link Accessed -> DataSubmitted -> Review -> Confirmed and STATUS_DATE stamped on every transition.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_candidate_record",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.3.1",
      "functional_specs": "Header form on table EMPONB_CANDIDATE_RECORD plus three detail (child) forms, each linked to the header by CANDIDATE_ID and ordered by LINE_NO: (a) Past Experience -> EMPONB_CAND_EXPERIENCE, (b) Educational Qualification -> EMPONB_CAND_EDUCATION, (c) Family -> EMPONB_CAND_FAMILY. STATUS lifecycle Link Generated -> Link Accessed -> DataSubmitted -> Review -> Confirmed with STATUS_DATE stamped on each transition. Header fields: HR capture (CANDIDATE_ID, CANDIDATE_NAME, GENDER, COUNTRY_CODE, DESIGN_CODE, EMAIL_ID, STATUS, STATUS_DATE, INITIATED_BY, INITIATED_ON), access key (ACCESS_KEY, KEY_GENERATED_ON, KEY_EXPIRY_DATETIME, KEY_VALID_FLAG, FORM_URL, LINK_SENT_ON, LINK_ACCESSED_ON, SUBMITTED_ON), candidate personal/contact/statutory/financial, validation status (PAN/AADHAR/BANK *_VALIDATED, *_VALIDATED_NAME, *_ATTEMPTS), attachments (PAN_DOC, AADHAR_DOC, BANK_DOC), HR finalization (EMP_CODE, DESIGNATION, DEPT_CODE, GRADE, CADRE, DESIGN_CODE, REPORT_TO, JOINED_AS, DATE_JOIN, WORK_SHIFT, HOL_TBLNO, EMP_SITE, PAY_SITE, BASIC, GROSS, PROBATION_DATE, PROBATION_PRD, NOTICE_PRD, EMAIL_ID_OFF, REPORT_TO__ADMIN, USER_ID, REMARKS, EMPLOYEE_PUSHED_FLAG, EMPLOYEE_PUSH_REF). Field validations: PAN AAAAA9999A, AADHAR 12 digits, IFSC 11-char, MOBILE 10 digits, PIN 6 digits, valid emails; KEY_EXPIRY_DATETIME = KEY_GENERATED_ON + :key_validity_days; EMP_CODE unique & DATE_JOIN mandatory & GROSS>=BASIC before Confirm; Confirm only when STATUS=Review. Actions: Search, List Recent, Add (Initiate Candidate), Edit, Delete (only while Link Generated and not accessed), Generate Access Key, Send Candidate Link (and Resend Link), Mark Review, Confirm Candidate (Push to IOFLOW Employee), Cancel Candidate. Triggers: send-email candidate link on Send Candidate Link, set STATUS=Review + STATUS_DATE on Mark Review, IOFLOW Employee-creation API + store EMPLOYEE_PUSHED_FLAG/EMPLOYEE_PUSH_REF + send-notification to HR on Confirm Candidate, STATUS reset and key invalidation on Cancel Candidate, set STATUS=DataSubmitted + invalidate key + notify on candidate Submit. On item_change of DESIGN_CODE, DEPT_CODE, DEPT_NAME, GRADE, GRADE_NAME, CADRE and CADRE_NAME are auto-filled from the matching EMPONB_DESIG_DEPT_MASTER row (matched on DESIGN_CODE) and shown read-only on the header. Selecting a Designation (DESIGN_CODE) on the header auto-fills Designation Name, Department Code, Department Name, Grade, Grade Name, Cadre and Cadre Name from the Designation & Department Master (EMPONB_DESIG_DEPT_MASTER), matched on DESIGN_CODE."
    },
    {
      "id": "emponb.3.2",
      "title": "Candidate Self",
      "parent_id": "emponb.3",
      "icon_image": "person_add",
      "description": "Candidate self-service onboarding: a header form plus four detail (child) forms - Past Experience, Educational Qualification, Family Details and Candidate Pay - that the candidate fills from the onboarding link, mirroring the same detail structure as the Candidate Onboarding Record.",
      "obj_name": "emponb_candidate_self",
      "obj_type": "T",
      "menu_path": "emponb.3.2",
      "functional_specs": "Candidate self-service onboarding record made up of a header form plus four detail (child) forms. Header form (table EMPONB_CANDIDATE_SELF) captures candidate identity, personal, contact, statutory and financial details plus access-key and validation status. CANDIDATE_ID is the key and must exist in EMPONB_CANDIDATE_RECORD (Candidate Onboarding Record). In addition to the header, the object has four detail child forms, each linked to the header by CANDIDATE_ID and ordered by LINE_NO: (a) Past Experience -> child table EMPONB_CAND_SELF_EXPERIENCE, (b) Educational Qualification -> child table EMPONB_CAND_SELF_EDUCATION, (c) Family Details -> child table EMPONB_CAND_SELF_FAMILY, (d) Candidate Pay -> child table EMPONB_CAND_SELF_PAY. All four detail forms render together with the header when the transaction is embedded (captured) on the candidate_page smart page, and the candidate fills these detail grids from the onboarding link - mirroring the same detail structure as emponb_candidate_record. item_change on CANDIDATE_ID loads the header from EMPONB_CANDIDATE_SELF, falling back to EMPONB_CANDIDATE_RECORD when no self record exists yet. The Past Experience detail (table EMPONB_CAND_SELF_EXPERIENCE) is pre-populated with the Past Experience lines HR already captured on the candidate record (table EMPONB_CAND_EXPERIENCE) for the same CANDIDATE_ID - seeded when HR sends/resends the onboarding link and also loaded into the grid when the form is opened for that CANDIDATE_ID. The candidate can review, edit, add or delete these lines before submitting. Existing field validations (PAN/AADHAR/IFSC/mobile/PIN/email formats, gender-relation combinations, no future Birth Date or Marriage Anniversary, email uniqueness) apply, and the submit_to_candidate_record action pushes the captured header and detail data back to the Candidate Onboarding Record. Search, Add, Edit, Delete. On successful completion of the Submit to HR action, STATUS is set to Submit and STATUS_DATE is stamped; once STATUS = Submit the record is locked and no further changes to any field are allowed. Includes a Same as Current Address checkbox on the header form that, when checked, copies CURRENT_ADDRESS, CURRENT_PIN, CURRENT_CITY and CURRENT_STATE into PERMANENT_ADDRESS, PERMANENT_PIN, PERMANENT_CITY and PERMANENT_STATE."
    },
